{{also|Tartar}}
==English==

===Etymology===
Via {{etyl|enm|en}}, via {{etyl|ML.|en}} from {{etyl|Medieval Greek|en}} {{term|τάρταρον|lang=grc|tr=tartaron}}, probably from {{etyl|ar|en}}{{rfscript|und|sc=Arab}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|tärʹ-tər}}, {{IPA|/ˈtɑr.tər/}}, {{X-SAMPA|/"tAr.t@r/}}
** {{a|UK}} {{IPA|[ˈtɑː.tə(ɹ)]}}
** {{a|US}} {{IPA|[ˈtɑɹ.ɾɚ]}}
* {{rhymes|ɑː(r)tə(r)}}
* {{hyphenation|tar|tar}}
* {{homophones|lang=en|tarter}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# A [[red]] [[compound]] [[deposited]] during [[wine]] [[making]]; mostly [[potassium]] [[hydrogen]] [[tartrate]] - a source of [[cream of tartar]].
# A [[hard]] [[yellow]] [[deposit]] on the [[teeth]].
# {{context|sometimes|capitalised}} A [[fearsome]] or angrily [[violent]] person.

